course: dictionary
lesson: 613
title: Axial: turning around a line
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Axial comes from axis, which is an imaginary line that something turns around, or that runs through its middle. A spinning top turns around its axis. So axial means "about an axis".
explain: The Earth turns around an imaginary line from the North Pole to the South Pole. This line is tilted, so Earth's axial tilt is about 23.5°. That tilt causes the seasons, because different parts of the Earth lean towards the Sun at different times of the year.
explain: Context helps, but not always. «Some historians call this the Axial Age» is a name for a period of history, not a description of something spinning. When the context does not give you the meaning, check the dictionary.
fact: Axis means an imaginary line through the middle of something, which it turns around.
fact: Axial means about an axis.
fact: Earth's axial tilt is about 23.5°, and it causes the seasons.
fact: Axial symmetry is reflection symmetry about a line: one half of a shape is a mirror image of the other half.
fact: In «the Axial Age», the word is a name that historians chose for a period of history, and some historians disagree that the pattern is neat.
exercise: «Earth's axial tilt causes the seasons.» What does axial mean? | Weather that changes quickly | Very old and dusty | Loud and noisy | *About an axis, the line something turns around
exercise: Maya says a shape has axial symmetry when one half is a mirror image of the other across a line. Is she right? | No, it means the shape has no sides | No, it means the shape is round | No, it means the shape is very large | *Yes, that is reflection symmetry about a line
exercise: Earth's axial tilt is about how far? | About 90° | About 180° | *About 23.5° | About 2.5°
test: A spinning top turns around a line through its middle. What is that line called? | A diagonal | *An axis | A radius | A vertex
test: Which describes axial rotation? | Moving in a straight line along a road | *Turning around an axis | Jumping up and down on one spot | Sitting still on a chair
exam: A pupil says, «The Axial Age was a time when everyone spun around.» Which answer is correct? | Axial means very old, so the Axial Age was a long time ago | *Axial means about an axis, so the name is not about spinning; the historians chose it as a label | Axial means loud, so the Axial Age was noisy | Axial means about an axis, so the Axial Age was a time of spinning
